<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-018 — Plateau tri-junction (120 degree) claim: Lami balance, periodic froth relaxation, junction-angle statistics — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`lami_angles_from_tensions` / `tensions_from_angles` / `thompson_fig113_cases` (L140-172) implement Thompson's triangle of forces exactly, `steiner_vs_cross_lengths` (L174-177) Lamarle's four-fold instability, and `PeriodicNetwork.energy_gradient` (L284-311) the Farhadifar-type vertex energy with orientation-dependent tension and an analytic gradient verified against finite differences in the self-test (L1267-1319). The equal-tension Plateau limit (Gamma = eps = 0) is now reached with combinatorial T1 exchanges (`t1_shortest_edge`, L345-406) and a gradient-norm convergence criterion (`relax_froth`, L440-465): the relaxed froth is three-valent with mean six sides, SD 9.9 degrees. What keeps it from the top band: edges are straight, so the model cannot reproduce the curved-film 120 degrees of a real froth in a disordered topology (documented in the claim boundary), and the 3D tetrahedral law is not simulated." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
