    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`plateau_statistics`, `bootstrap_vertex_ci`, `two_sample_ks` and `histogram_fit` (L180-232) deliver SD, RMS deviation, median |theta - 120| with vertex-resampled 95 % CIs, fraction within the a-priori +/-15 degree tolerance, CV, two-sample KS D/p, histogram Pearson r and RMSE; `goodness_of_fit` (L910-935) fits eps by KS distance and compares each specimen with the Plateau froth, the Poisson-Voronoi null and the Farhadifar comparator; `decide_verdict` (L937-973) applies the pre-registered criteria and records the branch-estimator robustness. The cornea result (KS p = 0.60 vs the froth, D = 0.27 vs Voronoi) is a genuine quantitative match. Deduction: the two estimators disagree on the cornea (7.2 vs 15.9 degrees), so the angle criterion is estimator-sensitive at the tolerance edge; no literature junction-angle distribution is available to pin as an external reference value." ;
