<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-018 — Plateau tri-junction (120 degree) claim: Lami balance, periodic froth relaxation, junction-angle statistics — Morphological realism / specimen match: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "All four specimens are loaded, verified (`verify_inputs`, L124-137) and segmented with pipelines matched to their imaging (`segment_specimen`, L532-572: nucleus-seeded watershed on a Sato ridge for the alizarin-red corneal mosaic, Sato wall mask + components for the magenta-walled onion, skeleton graph of the closed ink for Thompson's drawings, `skeleton_graph_analysis` L681-778), and the comparison figure (`render_figures`, L988-1109) shows each specimen with its segmentation and detected vertices beside the model and the nulls. The cornea segmentation is clean (126 cells, one nucleus each). Deductions: the onion pipeline drops small cells (47 of roughly 60 visible), and Fig. 124's four boundary T-junctions on the strip's outer walls are scored together with interior vertices." ;
